NOtes 

.Pagination
    .shows a slice of data instead of the whole table 
    .uses LIMIT and OFFSET to show data in pages 


.Aggregations 
    .summarizing many rows into one number 
    .functions like sum, count, average, min, max


.Joins 
    .combine related tables using matching keys 
    .where you have multiple different but related tables


.Subqueries 
    .query inside another query


.Stored procedures 
    .reusable blocks of code that can be called anytime
    .saved routines a DB can run automatically


.Views 
    .virtual table created from a query 
    .like a saved report that does not have to be rewritten everytime 


.Triggers
    .happen automatically when table events occur; are not manually run 
    .used for:
        .automatic validation
        .automatic calculations
        .automatic logging
        .automatic updates to related tables 
    .called by the DB


.Functions
    .built-in tools that take input - process it - return a value 
    they:
        .calculate values
        .transform text
        .manipulate dates 
        .perform math
        .aggregate data 
        .clean or format output 
    .they fall into:
            .aggregate functions
            .string functions
            .date functions
            .math functions
            .conditional functions 


.Clauses 
    .part of a QL statement that tells the DB how to process the query
    .comprise:
        .select - specifies which columns to return
        .from - specifies the table/s to query
        .where - filters rows based on conditions 
        .order by - sorts results ascending or descending 
        .group by - groups rows so aggregate functions can be applied 
        .having - filters grouped results 
                .used with GROUP BY
        .limit - restricts the number of rows returned 
        .offset - skips a number of rows before returning results 
        .join - combines rows from related tables 
        .distinct - returns only unique values 




.Statement 
    .complete instruction to give a DB
    .complete action like retrieve, insert, update, delete, create, modify, or control data 
    .comprise:
        .select - retrieves data from one or more tables
        .insert - add new rows to a table 
        .update - modify existing rows 
        .delete - delete rows from a table
        .create - create tables, views, procedures, triggers, DBs
        .alter - modify an existing table's structure 
        .drop - delete a table, view, or DB
        .truncate - delete all rows from a table but keep the structure 
        .use - select which DB to run statements against 
        .call - execute a stored procedure 
